    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear what you're saying about critical thinking, but it feels like you're saying the \"triumphs and shared values\" approach is fundamentally flawed or even \"fragile,\" while the other approach is the only way to achieve \"true\" cohesion. Is there really any merit to the idea that teaching children to be proud of their country's achievements is a valid and effective educational goal? Or is that approach just inherently regressive?",
